{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Moves items, markers and regions starting at or after the time selection start. One bar is intentionally four quarter notes (4/4), as in the original script. Automation and tempo markers are not moved. Back up your project first.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Generate passing chords between start and target chords, with automatic, ascending-step and descending-cycle modes, voicing previews and pagination. Requires REAPER with Lua ReaScript support and the ReaImGui extension (available through ReaPack). SWS is optional, for opening chord-reference URLs. Audition uses the virtual MIDI keyboard queue: enable track monitoring and select All MIDI inputs or Virtual MIDI keyboard as the track input.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Quantize selected MIDI items for notation using the native gfx options panel. Supports polyphonic/monophonic cleanup and optional copies on new tracks. Normalizes retained velocities to 100; removes CC-class events except pitch bend. Text, lyrics and SysEx are preserved. No extensions required.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Revoice selected notes independently in each editable MIDI-editor take. Native gfx chord panel, external-note strategies and collision-safe additions. REAPER 6/7, Lua 5.3+. No SWS/ReaPack dependencies.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Independent implementation using native REAPER APIs; no SWS required. Finds the first instrument on each selected track, then its nearest parent, then searches send destinations breadth-first (including their parents). Send traversal handles cycles. Shared instruments are processed once. If any resolved window is closed, show all; otherwise close all. This changes floating windows only, not FX bypass, offline state or routing.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Selected tracks with FX are shown in both TCP and mixer, with FX online. Unselected tracks with all FX offline are hidden. Tracks without FX are unchanged.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Independent native REAPER gfx calculator. No FX, SWS, ReaImGui or other dependencies. Beats are quarter-note beats (4 beats = one 4/4 bar); duration is in seconds. Convert beats + seconds to BPM, or beats + BPM to seconds. Tap with the mouse or Space. Tap intervals below 0.10 seconds are ignored; a gap over 3 seconds starts a new sequence. Average the latest 16 intervals. Space uses physical key-down edges to avoid keyboard auto-repeat taps. This utility never changes project tempo, transport, selection or media.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Manage persistent URL bookmarks from a mouse-position popup menu. Supports opening, adding, renaming, editing URLs, deleting, and reordering. Opening requires SWS CF_ShellExecute; only HTTP(S) and file URLs are allowed. File URLs use the system handler and must only point to trusted files.\par}
}
